branch: feature/optics-outside-chat-route
worktree: ../okay-wt-chat

why: two defects in one route, and it is the chat application's main
  endpoint (`Chat.chatRoute`, used by okay-demo and by Okay!Chat).

  (1) `r.url == "/chat"` compares the WHOLE request target, so
      `/chat?x=1` is a 404 — the same class the demo lane just fixed,
      live since e9901797 stopped Jetty dropping the query.
  (2) `messagesOf(r.body)` picks the conversation out by string
      literal and loses things SILENTLY: a body that is not JSON
      becomes `Vector.empty`, so the model answers an empty
      conversation with a 200; and a single message missing `role`,
      or carrying a non-string `content`, is DROPPED from the list —
      the model is handed a conversation with a hole in it and no one
      is told. That is worse than the empty case.

what: `Router.json[ChatRequest]` with
  `case class ChatRequest(messages: Vector[Anthropic.Message] = Vector.empty)`.
  `Anthropic.Message` already has a derived `Schema`.

  The default is deliberate: `{}` keeps answering as it does today
  (an empty conversation), while a body that does not PARSE is a 400
  instead of a reply to nothing. Malformed is refused; absent stays
  absent. A client sending `{}` is not broken by this lane.

first: a test that FAILS on master — a body with a hole reaches the
  model as a shorter conversation.

next: the failing test, the conversion, okay-demo's Live suite, docs
